pySMESH: build SMESH_Gen.cxx (SMESH V9_16_0) without Qt on Windows.

SMESH commit be238b4bb (2023-03-09, multinode parallel meshing) made SMESH_Gen.cxx include
<QString> and <QProcess> unconditionally. Their only user, SMESH_Gen::send_mesh, compiles its
body only #ifndef WIN32, and on WIN32 SMESH_Gen::parallelComputeSubMeshes throws
"ParallelMesh is not working on Windows". pySMESH builds without Qt, so this patch puts the two
includes under the same #ifndef WIN32 guard. No compiled code changes.

diff --git a/src/SMESH/SMESH_Gen.cxx b/src/SMESH/SMESH_Gen.cxx
index 24de572..c835f2a 100644
--- a/src/SMESH/SMESH_Gen.cxx
+++ b/src/SMESH/SMESH_Gen.cxx
@@ -51,8 +51,11 @@
 #include "memoire.h"
 #include <functional>
 
+// QString/QProcess serve only SMESH_Gen::send_mesh, whose body is #ifndef WIN32.
+#ifndef WIN32
 #include <QString>
 #include <QProcess>
+#endif
 
 #ifdef WIN32
   #include <windows.h>
